        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: St James Street, Monmouth, Monmouthshire, Wales\n- People: John Speed\n- Roles: cartographer, historian, mapmaker\n- Concepts: medieval town walls, Stuart period\n\nFacts:\n- John Speed was born in 1551 or 1552 and died on 28 July 1629.\n- John Speed was an English cartographer and historian.\n- John Speed is the best known English mapmaker of the Stuart period.\n- In 1610, John Speed made a map of Monmouth that showed St James Street as a segment of Whitecross Street.\n- St James Street is a historic street in the town centre of Monmouth, Monmouthshire, Wales.\n- St James Street is within the medieval town walls of Monmouth.",
